  <dashboards>
    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Desc. &amp; Introduction'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/WIPContentScoringv3/Desc_Introduction?rev=' id='Desc_Introduction' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/testContentScoringv3-skulevel' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='table'>
          <format attr='background-color' value='#666666' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1566' minheight='1000' minwidth='1566' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98400' id='68' layout-strategy-id='distribute-evenly' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98978' x='511' y='800'>
            <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98400' id='51' type-v2='text' w='98978' x='511' y='800'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='20' underline='true'>Introduction</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Content Completeness dashboard shows the completeness and quality measurement of each SKU based on some product attributes such as Title, Brand name, Barcode, Volumetrics etc. One of the main purposes of this dashboard is to enable content managers and other stakeholders in taking actions for the improvement of overall content score.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>There are 3 main bucktes that describes the content score. The Weighted Content Score follows the rules: 50% for User Experience, 20% Operations and 30% Quality. Where each bucket has the following composition:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Completeness User Experience: considering Completeness Title, Title Local, Description, Description Local, Image, Brand Name, Net Size.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Completeness Operations: considering Completeness L3 Master Category, Barcode, Weight, Volumetrics</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Quality: considering Quality Title, Image, Brand</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>There are aggregated scores that are consolidated according to each concept. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Completeness Volumetrics: Completeness Length, Completeness Width and Complenetess Height</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Net Size: Completeness Content Unit and Completeness Content Value</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>- Weight: Completeness Weight Unit and Completeness Weight Value</run>
                <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='20' underline='true'>Supporting Links</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Content Score Overview: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#4996b2' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1VASxKqkOHjJslkddA9f47_A01qH1kFiXh6TCC3YY-OA/edit#slide=id.g253bc7d9d94_0_388&amp;quot;'>https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1VASxKqkOHjJslkddA9f47_A01qH1kFiXh6TCC3YY-OA/edit#slide=id.g253bc7d9d94_0_388</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Content Score V3 definitions can be found here: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#4996b2' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-ISVB3xCk8Yi_dlsVFL9S9XM1UPmWNQ65BEcH-M9hkE/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;'>https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-ISVB3xCk8Yi_dlsVFL9S9XM1UPmWNQ65BEcH-M9hkE/edit?usp=sharing</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Changelog: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://confluence.deliveryhero.com/display/DINV/Content+Score+V3+Changelog&amp;quot;'>https://confluence.deliveryhero.com/display/DINV/Content+Score+V3+Changelog</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Confluence page link : </run>
                <run fontcolor='#4996b2' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://confluence.deliveryhero.com/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=570174669&amp;quot;'>https://confluence.deliveryhero.com/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=570174669</run>
                <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='20' underline='true'>Dashboard Description</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='14' underline='true'>Average Scores</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>This tab gives insights on different levels (Global, Regional, and Management Entity). It shows the Avg. Scores from the latest week&apos;s data. This page does not have any dimensions or filters. It only shows the snapshot of the current status.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='15' underline='true'>Historical view - Scores</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>This page shows the Weighted Content, User Experience, Operations and Quality scores over time in a tabular format.  Users can select the date range given next to the filters.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Geo- Granularity</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>: This historical view does not have dimensions because the values are pre-calculated in SQL code prior to feeding it to the tableau. However, Geo-granularity gives users the flexibility to view the scores on different data granularity. For example, if the user selects &quot;Region&quot; in Geo-granularity then the dashboard will show the scores on a regional level. Similarly, if a user wants to see the score for a different country with its product type then the user should select &quot;Country - Product Type&quot;.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Filters</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>: Users can select Region, Country, Product Tupe, Dmart and the desired date</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='14' underline='true'>Historical view - Sub scores</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>This page shows not only the Weighted Content, User Experience, Operations and Quality scores but also the subsocres considered for each of them. For instance; Completeness Tile, Completeness description, Quality Title, Completeness Volumetrics etc. This tab also show the scores over time in a tabular format, users can select the date range given next to the filters.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Geo- Granularity</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>: Similar to the dashboard description of Historical view - Scores.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Filters</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>: Users can select Region, Country, Product Tupe, Dmart and the desired date</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='14' underline='true'>SKU Level Scores</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>This Page shows the SKU level data with all scores associated with it in a tabular form. There are no dimensions used in this view. Usage of filters is the same as described in the previous two dashboard descriptions.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Note</run>
                <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>: User must filter and select only one country at a time to see the all SKUs with their scores and subscores. </run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='470' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='469' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98400' id='51' type-v2='text' w='98978' x='511' y='800'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='20' underline='true'>Introduction</run>
